TAL_UNITS statistics on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY with `TOTAL_UNITS > 0` (+ enrollment filter): 3 precedents — dw_1212, dw_3644, dw_1335(Subquery2).\n- TOTAL_UNITS statistics on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED with IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM='Y' for Mathematics per academic year: 1 precedent — dw_1023 (but it pairs with SUBJECT_SUMMARY enrollment, and its question names catalog-only attributes \"not variable units\", absent from our question).\n- NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS variance/stddev per academic year via ACADEMIC_TERMS join: dw_2958 (SUBJECT_OFFERED), dw_4527 (SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TERM_CODE LIKE).\n- CV precedents: dw_2180 (SUBJECT_SUMMARY units), dw_4640 (TIP enrollment) — both `STDDEV/AVG` shape.\n- Range+variance of enrolled students precedent: dw_1350 (MAX−MIN, VARIANCE).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\nSUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY is the subject-grain registrar rollup consumed by 39 metrics for enrollment and unit statistics per department/term/year (dw_1212, dw_3644, dw_4527, dw_1335 etc.). ACADEMIC_TERMS is the standard enrichment dimension attaching ACADEMIC_YEAR/ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC to offering facts (dw_1023, dw_2958, dw_4701). COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves catalog-attribute questions (flags, grading, HGN). SUBJECT_SUMMARY serves official-enrollment questions (\"subject enrollment number\").\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\nAll Phase-1 entities investigated: tables SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (semantic_get + graph neighbors + metrics_by_table for SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY); column concepts total_units, enrollment_measures, term_code, year_columns, subject_id, department_name, master_subject_id (semantic_get / graph); concepts subject_offering_facts, academic_term_dimension (semantic_get); metrics dw_1023, dw_2180, dw_4640, dw_1350, dw_2958, dw_1212, dw_3644, dw_1335, dw_3311, dw_4527, dw_4701, dw_1301, dw_41, dw_2272, dw_2580, dw_1393, dw_4229, dw_2398, dw_5150, dw_4566, dw_3268, dw_4184, dw_3632, dw_3530, dw_1766, dw_2158 (semantic_get for SQL). Unrelated results (facilities/HR/Moira/IAP-only entities) discarded per screening. **mysql_query could not be executed — persistent `Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'` environment error despite many retries; verification by execution was impossible.**\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** (only table with both `TOTAL_UNITS` and `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` at subject grain — 3b), filtered by `OFFER_DEPT_NAME='Mathematics'` and `TERM_CODE LIKE '%FA'` (fall — 3c), joined to **ACADEMIC_TERMS** on TERM_CODE for `ACADEMIC_YEAR`/`ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`. The question describes two distinct populations (units>0 for the CV; enrolled>0 for range/variance — the wording attaches each filter to its own measure and says \"those courses\" for the variance), so compute two CTEs joined on ACADEMIC_YEAR (dw_1023/dw_4701 two-CTE-join precedent).\n\n**6b.** CV = `STDDEV(TOTAL_UNITS)/AVG(TOTAL_UNITS)` (bare STDDEV per tip; dw_4640 shape); range = `MAX(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)-MIN(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` (dw_1350); variance = `VARIANCE(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` (dw_2958). No rounding. SELECT exactly 5 columns in asked order. Caveat: single-population (both filters in one WHERE) is the alternative reading; the distributive filter wording and the dw_1212 joint-parenthetical counter-example favor two populations (6d).\n\n**6c.** Data: subject-grain table avoids section fan-out; both measure columns physically exist (columns definition). Semantic-network: enrollment/total_units decision guides both route to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY; ACADEMIC_TERMS join edge documented. Business: dw_1212/dw_3644/dw_1335 precedent filters (`TOTAL_UNITS>0`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS>=1`) on this exact table; dw_2958 precedent for per-year enrollment variance via ACADEMIC_TERMS.\n\n**6d.** Alternatives: (i) single-pass with both filters — would change the CV population; tie-breaker would be running both against data (impossible here due to the DB auth failure); the faithful-wording argument favors two populations. (ii) catalog-based CV (dw_1023 style) — rejected because the question names no catalog-only attribute and pairs both populations identically.\n\n",
